The fix is in place. Here's a summary of what was done:

## Problem
In `src/CAC.ts`, the `mri` method was applying the option's `default` value to **every alias name** unconditionally. When a user passed only one alias (e.g. `--base-url https://gitlab.com`), the parsed value overwrote the default for that one name, but the other alias (`b`) was left holding the default value.

## Fix
Modified the default-application loop in `mri` to first check whether **any** of the option's alias names was actually present in the parsed result. If yes, no defaults are applied (parsed values will be set later in the existing loop); if no, the default is still applied to all alias names (preserving the existing "default value without args" semantics).

```ts
const hasParsedName = cliOption.names.some(
  (name) => parsed[name] !== undefined
)
if (!hasParsedName) {
  for (const name of cliOption.names) {
    options[name] = cliOption.config.default
  }
}
```

## Verification
- All 4 existing tests pass (including the "default value without args" test which requires `b` and `baseUrl` to both be set to the default when no args are parsed).
- The bug case (`--base-url https://gitlab.com`) now correctly leaves `b` as `undefined` instead of leaking the default `https://github.com`.
- The other direction (`-b https://gitlab.com`) still works correctly because mri populates both `b` and `baseUrl` keys via the configured alias.

